290	/**
291	 * The sheet's settings: its clerk limit (none: no limit) and its floor, the least a claim's live due
292	 * can be, and its terms, the days after its date a claim is due by, and its late percent, what an
293	 * overdue claim gains of its figure for every full 30 days overdue. Changing the floor or the late
294	 * percent moves the figures, so the figures that move are recorded. Its policy date (none:
295	 * the sheet's today) decides how a claim's live figures round (see {@link Rounding}), so changing it
296	 * records the figures that move too. Its period-numbering-from date (none: off) decides how a claim
297	 * opened is numbered: on or after it, within its period (see {@link SheetService#nextClaimNumber}).
298	 * Its cap (none: no cap) is the most a person's due-total can be, so changing it records the
299	 * figures that move too. A grade may have its own terms; a grade without uses the sheet's terms. A claim's due-by is fixed
300	 * when it is created, so changing any terms moves no claim's due-by. A grade may have grace days (none: no grace): a
301	 * claim whose person's grade on its date has grace days on that date is overdue only once its due-by plus them is
302	 * before the sheet's today, and its late charge counts its 30-day boundaries from there (see
303	 * {@link Sheet#lateFrom}); its due-by is unchanged. Changing a grade's grace days moves the figures, so the figures
304	 * that move are recorded.
305	 * <p>
306	 * The settings that carry a figure (the floor, the late percent, the terms, a grade's own terms,
307	 * a grade's grace days, the clerk limit, the cap, the proof threshold, a grade's own proof threshold and the note threshold) are dated: each value is recorded from a from-date (the sheet's
308	 * today when none is given). A claim's floor and late percent are those in force on its
309	 * date (its terms are those in force on the day it was created: the sheet's today then), as is its proof threshold (its person's grade's own in force then when it has one, else the sheet's; see {@link Sheet#proofThresholdFor}) and its note threshold (see {@link Sheet#noteThresholdOn}) and its review threshold (see {@link Sheet#reviewThresholdOn}); the clerk limit and the cap are those in force on the sheet's today (see {@link Sheet}).
310	 * The policy date and the period-numbering-from date are not dated. Nor is the permission matrix:
311	 * for each of open, settle, void, reassign, close and reopen, the roles that may take it (blank: the
312	 * standing rule, see {@link Sheet#permits}), recorded under the key {@code perm-<action>}. Nor are
313	 * the grace days (none: off): when the sheet's today changes, every open period whose to-date plus
314	 * the grace days is before the new today is closed (see {@link SheetService#setToday}). Nor is the
315	 * entry date (none: off): while set, it is the default date of a new claim in place of the sheet's today.
316	 * Nor is the pot (none: no pot), shared out over each balanced pool's members as their cuts (see
317	 * {@link net.officefloor.hq.app.pool.PoolService}). Nor is the parent (none: no parent), a sheet that has
318	 * been loaded, never the sheet itself nor one that has it as an ancestor: a grade with no rate in force on a date
319	 * here takes its parent's, then the parent's parent's, up to three levels up (see {@link RateChain}), so changing it
320	 * records the figures that move too. Nor are the proof kinds (none: off): while set, a claim above its proof threshold needs a proof of each
321	 * before it can be settled or approved. Nor is the alert threshold (none: off): a change whose figures
322	 * lift a person's due-total above it records an ALERT (see {@link RollupService#recordChanges}); changing
323	 * it moves no figures. The rounding mode (none: off) is dated like the floor: a claim whose date has
324	 * one in force rounds its live figures by it in place of the policy date (see {@link Rounding}), so
325	 * changing it records the figures that move too.
326	 */
