388	    /**
389	     * Save the settings given: a clerk limit when {@code limit} is not null, and the floor, the
390	     * terms and the late percent when they are not null, and a policy date when {@code changePolicy}
391	     * (null for none), and a period-numbering-from date when {@code changeNumbering} (null for off),
392	     * and a cap when {@code cap} is not null, and each grade's own terms given in {@code gradeTerms}
393	     * (by grade, in grade order), and each grade's grace days given in {@code gradeGraces} (by grade, in grade
394	     * order; null for none), and a proof threshold when {@code proofThreshold} is not null, and each grade's own proof
395	     * threshold given in {@code gradeProofThresholds} (by grade, in grade order; null for none), and a note threshold when
396	     * {@code noteThreshold} is not null, and a review threshold when {@code reviewThreshold} is not null, and each permission matrix entry
397	     * given in {@code permissions} (by action, in the order given; blank for the standing rule), and the grace days when
398	     * {@code changeGrace} (null for off), and the entry date when {@code changeEntry} (null for off), and the pot when {@code changePot} (null for none), and the parent when
399	     * {@code changeParent} (null for none; refused (400) for the sheet itself, a sheet never loaded, or one that has
400	     * this sheet as an ancestor, before anything is saved), and the fiscal start month when {@code fiscalStartMonth}
401	     * is not null (1 to 12; anything else refused (400) before anything is saved), and the alert threshold when
402	     * {@code changeAlert} (null for off), and the rounding mode when {@code rounding} is not null (half-up or
403	     * half-even, null for none; anything else refused (400) before anything is saved), and the escalation gap when
404	     * {@code changeEscalate} (null for off), and the review SLA when {@code changeReviewSla} (null for none), and the proof kinds when {@code changeProofKinds} (comma separated, null for none). Each figure is recorded from its from-date, keeping the values
405	     * already recorded (one already recorded from that date is replaced). Each one saved is
406	     * recorded, in that order.
